        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. India: Modi wants Indians to stop buying gold Asia / Pacific Issued on: 11/05/2026 - 18:06 Modified: 11/05/2026 - 18:22 Narendra #Modi's message to Indians is clear: stop buying gold jewellery for a year. With #India having to pay more to import #oil due to the #Iranwar, its prime minister hopes that holding off on buying the precious metal will protect the country's trade balance - a decision that could badly hit a nearly $100 billion industry. At least 15 killed in car bomb attack on northwest Pakistan checkpoint 10/05/2026 Asia / Pacific At least three killed by volcano eruption in Indonesia 08/05/2026 Asia / Pacific China's 'key priorities': Open Hormuz, get oil flowing, avoid 'getting dragged into conflicts' 06/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Iranian and Chinese FMS meet as Beijing urges countries to maintain ceasefire 06/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi in push to revise pacifist constitution 06/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Japanese PM Takaichi in push to revise pacifist constitution as regional tensions rise 05/05/2026 Asia / Pacific ‘Far beyond’ EU and NATO: Armenia hosts EPC summit cast as ‘gateway’ in shifting diplomatic order 04/05/2026 Europe Foreign minister signals new era for Armenia: Peace, EU ambitions, trade, 'huge' infrastructure plan 29/04/2026 Asia / Pacific Pirate gangs prowl Bangladesh's Sundarbans forest 24/04/2026 Asia / Pacific"
