        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Starmer pledges to bring Britain closer to the EU as he faces calls to step down Issued on: 11/05/2026 - 17:24 Modified: 11/05/2026 - 17:31 UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer pledged Monday to prove the “doubters” in his own party and among the electorate as a whole wrong as he tries to fight off demands to step down after devastating local election results for his Labour Party. Starmer argued that he will “face up to the big challenges” and restore hope to the country, in part by forging closer ties with the European Union, six years after the UK's acrimonious departure from the bloc. FRANCE 24's European Affairs Editor Armen Georgian tells us more. Hantavirus outbreak: Should we worry about the virus spreading? 11/05/2026 Africa Forward Summit in Kenya: France offers ‘third way’ in Africa’s AI race 11/05/2026 Ukraine and Russia fight on despite US-mediated ceasefire 11/05/2026 Hantavirus: France enforces strict measures after citizen tests positive 11/05/2026 Hantavirus: French PM Lecornu holds talks with medical advisers, ministers 11/05/2026 Changing geopolitics, deals and new partnerships on the menu at Africa-France summit 11/05/2026 'I will make order': Macorn calls for silence at Africa summit 11/05/2026 Africa Hantavirus ship evacuation nears completion as 94 flown home 11/05/2026 UK's Starmer promises to be bolder to try to rescue his job 11/05/2026"
